TDOC: GAIA-WINDOWS-NODE
VERSION: 1.0.0
MODE: AUDIT-FIRST

PURPOSE
Define the stable command contract for the Gaia Windows worker.

COMMANDS

inventory
  Read-only hardware, OS, network, services, scheduled-task, startup, Git, and storage inventory.

repository-audit
  Read-only scan for tracked binaries, dotfiles, oversized objects, suspicious filenames, credential patterns, and repository drift.

network-audit
  Read-only interface, DNS, gateway, route, proxy, firewall, latency, and packet-loss assessment.

sentinel-status
  Read-only health status for Sentinel-managed processes and queues.

telemetry-status
  Read-only local queue depth, oldest event, last successful push, and last error.

optimize-plan
  Produce a proposed optimization plan. No changes are made.

optimize-apply
  Apply only explicitly approved optimization actions and emit before/after telemetry.

sync-status
  Report Git branch, commit, working-tree state, and upstream relationship.

recovery
  Validate rollback/recovery prerequisites without modifying protected data.

CAPABILITY RULES
- Default capability is read-only.
- Destructive operations require explicit operator authorization.
- Secrets are never printed to stdout or telemetry.
- Telemetry contains metadata, not arbitrary file contents.
- Every state-changing command emits a correlation ID.
- Failed commands return non-zero status and preserve diagnostic context locally.

TELEMETRY EVENT
{
  "event_id": "uuid",
  "timestamp": "RFC3339",
  "node": "windows-gaia",
  "command": "tdoc-command",
  "mode": "audit|change|recovery",
  "result": "ok|warning|error",
  "correlation_id": "uuid",
  "previous_hash": "sha256",
  "event_hash": "sha256"
}
